- \( R \) is the radius of the Sun in cm.
- \( \sigma \) is the Stefan-Boltzmann constant, which is approximately \( 5.67 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{erg/cm}^2 \cdot \text{s}^4 \cdot \text{K}^4 \).
- \( T_e \) is the effective temperature of the Sun in Kelvin.

